# Tutorials for the games. Each story is one tutorial in the docs and one acceptance test.

Story: Your first pylon race
  As a pilot
  I want to race other planes round the pylons
  So that I can practise fast, tight turns against somebody

  A [[pylon race]] is five laps of a triangle of three pylons, against three
  [[computer pilots]]. In this tutorial, you start a race, throw at GO and fly the five laps.
  At the end, the game panel shows your place and your time.

  Scenario: Start, throw at GO, fly five laps
    When the pilot starts a race
    Then the game is a race
    When the countdown ends
    Then the game clock is running
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot flies the race
    Then the lap count is 5
    And the game clock is stopped

Story: A game of tag
  As a pilot
  I want to chase other planes, and get away from them
  So that I can practise to fly near other planes

  In a game of [[tag]], the plane that is [[it]] chases the others. You are it first. In
  this tutorial, you tag a computer pilot. Then that pilot chases you, until it tags you
  back.

  Scenario: Tag, then get tagged
    When the pilot starts a game of tag
    Then the chaser is you
    When the countdown ends
    Then the opponents are flying
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot tags an opponent
    Then the chaser is an opponent
    When the chaser tags the plane
    Then the chaser is you
